# User interactions doc is the contract

`docs/user-interactions.md` is the plain-language source of truth for Files page and toolbar UX (what the user does, what the app should do, what it must not do).

## Do not break

When changing `app.js`, `app.html`, `base.html`, objects/projects APIs, or related services:

1. **Read the relevant section** of `docs/user-interactions.md` before changing behavior.
2. Preserve documented “App should” / “App must not” rows (especially: folder name opens / row chrome selects; Remove from Project clears the row without hard refresh; navigating folders keeps Creo connected; empty folders stay removable).
3. Prefer updating matching regression tests in the same change when behavior is intentional.

## Keep the doc updated

When the user asks for a UX / toolbar / Files-list / Add / Checkout / Check In / Remove / open / soft-nav change (or you change those behaviors):

1. **Edit `docs/user-interactions.md` in the same change** — keep the **You do / App should / App must not** tables accurate; update walkthroughs if needed.
2. Write for testers first (plain language). Put test file pointers only in the short “For developers” section.
3. Do not leave the doc describing old menus, click rules, or stale “must not” rows.

## Examples

```text
# ✅ GOOD — rename Check In menu items → update labels/order in the doc + tests
# ✅ GOOD — fix remove list refresh → keep Remove from Project “must not leave row until F5”
# ❌ BAD — change folder click to always select, leave doc saying name opens
# ❌ BAD — ship Add mode behavior change without touching user-interactions.md
```
